#Rigid-group definitions for the springs-only rotamer/hinge mechanism: all DOF
#together (backbone phi/psi/omega, side-chain chi1..chi4, hydroxyl/thiol
#rotation).
#
#Same columnar syntax as the coarse-grain reduce rules (name resname atom1
#atom2 ...), reusing the same reader, but the ".rbody" extension marks that
#the two are read differently: a .grp line reduces its atoms into one output
#grain, a .rbody line instead creates every pairwise spring between its atoms
#and leaves the particles distinct -- nothing is reduced or merged.
#Adjacent groups overlap on exactly the 2 atoms of a hinge axis -- that overlap
#alone gives "2 anchors, 1 free rotation", nothing else needed.
#
#CHARMM-style +/- prefix: "+X"/"-X" means atom X of the next/previous residue
#in the chain, instead of the current one. A rule's resname always refers to
#its own (unprefixed) residue, matched regardless of what +/- neighbour it is.
#
#Naming <ResidueCode>_<Part>: _CA = CA tetrahedron.
#
#DIFFERENCE FROM ProteinAtomRigidGroups.rbody (the base file this is derived
#from): there, _PHI = the WHOLE peptide plane behind this residue
#{-CA, -C, -O, N, H, CA} as one single rigid clique -- besides giving phi its
#hinge (overlap with _CA on {N, CA}), that clique also directly springs
#{-CA, -O} (upstream of the -C-N peptide bond) to {H, CA} (downstream of it),
#which freezes the OMEGA dihedral (rotation around -C-N) as an unwanted side
#effect, at the uniform --stiffness value -- omega never gets to be governed
#by --bondedinteraction's real, much softer AMBER torsion term, since the
#uniform rigid-body spring dominates it completely. Here, _PHI is split into
#two halves at exactly that -C/N hinge:
#  _PHIC = {-CA, -C, -O, N}    (upstream half: rigid with the PREVIOUS
#                               residue's own carbonyl, N is only a shared
#                               hinge anchor here, not sprung to anything
#                               downstream of it)
#  _PHIN = {-C, N, H, CA}      (downstream half: rigid with THIS residue's
#                               own amide, -C is only a shared hinge anchor)
#These two overlap on exactly {-C, N} -- the omega(i-1,i) hinge, same "2
#anchors, 1 free rotation" trick already used for phi/psi/chi. Springing an
#anchor atom (-C or N) to the OTHER half's own substituents is harmless (it
#only pins a 1-3 angle through the shared atom, e.g. -C-N-CA, which doesn't
#depend on the rotation angle around -C-N at all) -- what must never happen,
#and no longer does, is a DIRECT spring between a non-anchor atom on one side
#(-CA, -O) and a non-anchor atom on the other (H, CA), which is exactly what
#depends on omega and must stay free. _PSI is split the same way, at the
#NEXT residue's omega(i,i+1) hinge {C, +N}:
#  _PSIC = {CA, C, O, +N}      (upstream half, overlaps _CA on {CA, C}: the
#                               psi axis, unaffected by this split)
#  _PSIN = {C, +N, +H, +CA}    (downstream half)
#_PHIC(i) and _PSIC(i-1) are the same 4 atoms (ditto _PHIN(i)/_PSIN(i-1)),
#deliberately written twice (once from each residue, exactly like the base
#file's _PHI(i)/_PSI(i-1) redundancy) so terminus handling (see below) still
#works per-residue without any special-casing. First/last residue in a chain
#is missing -CA/-C/-O or +N/+H/+CA respectively: skip rather than fail. Same
#for +H when the next residue is proline (no amide H). ACE/NME's own
#ACE_C/NME_N groups already only reach the shared hinge atom itself (never
#the OTHER residue's own H/CA substituents), so they needed no change here --
#the over-constraint only ever came from the full, unsplit _PHI/_PSI cliques.
#
#Consequence: omega is now exactly as free (uniform --stiffness only, no
#real physics yet) as phi/psi/chi already are without --bondedinteraction --
#a real AMBER omega DIHEDRAL/GHOSTPARTICLE family in a .bi.ff can now
#restrain it realistically instead of it being pre-frozen at whatever value
#the input structure happened to have. NOT YET VALIDATED for dynamics
#stability (a new free hinge, softer than before) -- test before relying on
#this the way --rigidbody alone has already been validated.
#
#_CB.._SD = chi1..4 pivots down the side chain. _RING/_GUAN = rigid
#aromatic/imidazole/guanidinium terminus. _SG/_OG/_OG1/_OH = hydroxyl/thiol
#pivot, {axis atom1, axis atom2, H} only -- the heavy atom stays in its parent
#group, only the H rotates.
#
#_NTER/_CTER: only needed for the chain's actual first/last residue, where
#_PHIC/_PHIN/_PSIC/_PSIN don't form (no -/+ neighbour). NTER's N carries
#NH3+ (H1/H2/H3) instead of the single amide H used everywhere else; CTER's
#C carries COO- (O, OXT) instead of the single carbonyl O -- both left
#unconstrained otherwise, so these two groups are not optional for a
#terminal residue.
#
#Assumes all-atom + H (PDB v3 naming). Pro is one rigid ring (side chain
#closes onto backbone N) plus its own _PHIC/_PHIN/_PSIC/_PSIN/_NTER/_CTER
#(_PHIN has no H, Pro's N has none in the amide position); as NTER, its ring
#nitrogen keeps CD and gets only 2 extra H (H2, H3), not 3. Terminal methyls
#(Ala CB, Ile/Thr/Val branch) included for completeness though not a real
#chi.

A_CA ALA N CA C CB HA
A_NTER ALA N CA H1 H2 H3
A_CTER ALA CA C O OXT
A_PHIC ALA -CA -C -O N
A_PHIN ALA -C N H CA
A_PSIC ALA CA C O +N
A_PSIN ALA C +N +H +CA
A_CB ALA CA CB HB1 HB2 HB3

R_CA ARG N CA C CB HA
R_NTER ARG N CA H1 H2 H3
R_CTER ARG CA C O OXT
R_PHIC ARG -CA -C -O N
R_PHIN ARG -C N H CA
R_PSIC ARG CA C O +N
R_PSIN ARG C +N +H +CA
R_CB ARG CA CB CG HB2 HB3
R_CG ARG CB CG CD HG2 HG3
R_CD ARG CG CD NE HD2 HD3
R_NE ARG CD NE CZ HE
R_GUAN ARG NE CZ NH1 NH2 HH11 HH12 HH21 HH22

N_CA ASN N CA C CB HA
N_NTER ASN N CA H1 H2 H3
N_CTER ASN CA C O OXT
N_PHIC ASN -CA -C -O N
N_PHIN ASN -C N H CA
N_PSIC ASN CA C O +N
N_PSIN ASN C +N +H +CA
N_CB ASN CA CB CG HB2 HB3
N_CG ASN CB CG OD1 ND2 HD21 HD22

D_CA ASP N CA C CB HA
D_NTER ASP N CA H1 H2 H3
D_CTER ASP CA C O OXT
D_PHIC ASP -CA -C -O N
D_PHIN ASP -C N H CA
D_PSIC ASP CA C O +N
D_PSIN ASP C +N +H +CA
D_CB ASP CA CB CG HB2 HB3
D_CG ASP CB CG OD1 OD2

C_CA CYS N CA C CB HA
C_NTER CYS N CA H1 H2 H3
C_CTER CYS CA C O OXT
C_PHIC CYS -CA -C -O N
C_PHIN CYS -C N H CA
C_PSIC CYS CA C O +N
C_PSIN CYS C +N +H +CA
C_CB CYS CA CB SG HB2 HB3
C_SG CYS CB SG HG

Q_CA GLN N CA C CB HA
Q_NTER GLN N CA H1 H2 H3
Q_CTER GLN CA C O OXT
Q_PHIC GLN -CA -C -O N
Q_PHIN GLN -C N H CA
Q_PSIC GLN CA C O +N
Q_PSIN GLN C +N +H +CA
Q_CB GLN CA CB CG HB2 HB3
Q_CG GLN CB CG CD HG2 HG3
Q_CD GLN CG CD OE1 NE2 HE21 HE22

E_CA GLU N CA C CB HA
E_NTER GLU N CA H1 H2 H3
E_CTER GLU CA C O OXT
E_PHIC GLU -CA -C -O N
E_PHIN GLU -C N H CA
E_PSIC GLU CA C O +N
E_PSIN GLU C +N +H +CA
E_CB GLU CA CB CG HB2 HB3
E_CG GLU CB CG CD HG2 HG3
E_CD GLU CG CD OE1 OE2

G_CA GLY N CA C HA2 HA3
G_NTER GLY N CA H1 H2 H3
G_CTER GLY CA C O OXT
G_PHIC GLY -CA -C -O N
G_PHIN GLY -C N H CA
G_PSIC GLY CA C O +N
G_PSIN GLY C +N +H +CA

H_CA HIS N CA C CB HA
H_NTER HIS N CA H1 H2 H3
H_CTER HIS CA C O OXT
H_PHIC HIS -CA -C -O N
H_PHIN HIS -C N H CA
H_PSIC HIS CA C O +N
H_PSIN HIS C +N +H +CA
H_CB HIS CA CB CG HB2 HB3
H_RING HIS CB CG ND1 CD2 CE1 NE2 HD1 HD2 HE1 HE2

I_CA ILE N CA C CB HA
I_NTER ILE N CA H1 H2 H3
I_CTER ILE CA C O OXT
I_PHIC ILE -CA -C -O N
I_PHIN ILE -C N H CA
I_PSIC ILE CA C O +N
I_PSIN ILE C +N +H +CA
I_CB ILE CA CB CG1 CG2 HB
I_CG1 ILE CB CG1 CD1 HG12 HG13
I_CG2 ILE CB CG2 HG21 HG22 HG23
I_CD1 ILE CG1 CD1 HD11 HD12 HD13

L_CA LEU N CA C CB HA
L_NTER LEU N CA H1 H2 H3
L_CTER LEU CA C O OXT
L_PHIC LEU -CA -C -O N
L_PHIN LEU -C N H CA
L_PSIC LEU CA C O +N
L_PSIN LEU C +N +H +CA
L_CB LEU CA CB CG HB2 HB3
L_CG LEU CB CG CD1 CD2 HG
L_CD1 LEU CG CD1 HD11 HD12 HD13
L_CD2 LEU CG CD2 HD21 HD22 HD23

K_CA LYS N CA C CB HA
K_NTER LYS N CA H1 H2 H3
K_CTER LYS CA C O OXT
K_PHIC LYS -CA -C -O N
K_PHIN LYS -C N H CA
K_PSIC LYS CA C O +N
K_PSIN LYS C +N +H +CA
K_CB LYS CA CB CG HB2 HB3
K_CG LYS CB CG CD HG2 HG3
K_CD LYS CG CD CE HD2 HD3
K_CE LYS CD CE NZ HE2 HE3
K_NZ LYS CE NZ HZ1 HZ2 HZ3

M_CA MET N CA C CB HA
M_NTER MET N CA H1 H2 H3
M_CTER MET CA C O OXT
M_PHIC MET -CA -C -O N
M_PHIN MET -C N H CA
M_PSIC MET CA C O +N
M_PSIN MET C +N +H +CA
M_CB MET CA CB CG HB2 HB3
M_CG MET CB CG SD HG2 HG3
M_SD MET CG SD CE
M_CE MET SD CE HE1 HE2 HE3

F_CA PHE N CA C CB HA
F_NTER PHE N CA H1 H2 H3
F_CTER PHE CA C O OXT
F_PHIC PHE -CA -C -O N
F_PHIN PHE -C N H CA
F_PSIC PHE CA C O +N
F_PSIN PHE C +N +H +CA
F_CB PHE CA CB CG HB2 HB3
F_RING PHE CB CG CD1 CD2 CE1 CE2 CZ HD1 HD2 HE1 HE2 HZ

#Note: P_PHI/P_RING deliberately never connect "-C" to CD (the real
#(-C)-N-CD angle, from the ring closing onto N instead of an amide H, is
#the actual physical restriction on Pro's phi). It's added by
#--bondedinteraction alone (BondedForceFieldReader's fallback spring, with
#the real AMBER angle constant), not here: a uniform --stiffness spring
#with no real angle constant would freeze phi completely instead of
#realistically restricting it -- see IO/BondedForceFieldReader.h.
P_RING PRO N CA C CB CG CD HA HB2 HB3 HG2 HG3 HD2 HD3
P_NTER PRO N CA CD H2 H3
P_CTER PRO CA C O OXT
P_PHIC PRO -CA -C -O N
P_PHIN PRO -C N CA
P_PSIC PRO CA C O +N
P_PSIN PRO C +N +H +CA

S_CA SER N CA C CB HA
S_NTER SER N CA H1 H2 H3
S_CTER SER CA C O OXT
S_PHIC SER -CA -C -O N
S_PHIN SER -C N H CA
S_PSIC SER CA C O +N
S_PSIN SER C +N +H +CA
S_CB SER CA CB OG HB2 HB3
S_OG SER CB OG HG

T_CA THR N CA C CB HA
T_NTER THR N CA H1 H2 H3
T_CTER THR CA C O OXT
T_PHIC THR -CA -C -O N
T_PHIN THR -C N H CA
T_PSIC THR CA C O +N
T_PSIN THR C +N +H +CA
T_CB THR CA CB OG1 CG2 HB
T_OG1 THR CB OG1 HG1
T_CG2 THR CB CG2 HG21 HG22 HG23

W_CA TRP N CA C CB HA
W_NTER TRP N CA H1 H2 H3
W_CTER TRP CA C O OXT
W_PHIC TRP -CA -C -O N
W_PHIN TRP -C N H CA
W_PSIC TRP CA C O +N
W_PSIN TRP C +N +H +CA
W_CB TRP CA CB CG HB2 HB3
W_RING TRP CB CG CD1 CD2 NE1 CE2 CE3 CZ2 CZ3 CH2 HD1 HE1 HE3 HZ2 HZ3 HH2

Y_CA TYR N CA C CB HA
Y_NTER TYR N CA H1 H2 H3
Y_CTER TYR CA C O OXT
Y_PHIC TYR -CA -C -O N
Y_PHIN TYR -C N H CA
Y_PSIC TYR CA C O +N
Y_PSIN TYR C +N +H +CA
Y_CB TYR CA CB CG HB2 HB3
Y_RING TYR CB CG CD1 CD2 CE1 CE2 CZ OH HD1 HD2 HE1 HE2
Y_OH TYR CZ OH HH

V_CA VAL N CA C CB HA
V_NTER VAL N CA H1 H2 H3
V_CTER VAL CA C O OXT
V_PHIC VAL -CA -C -O N
V_PHIN VAL -C N H CA
V_PSIC VAL CA C O +N
V_PSIN VAL C +N +H +CA
V_CB VAL CA CB CG1 CG2 HB
V_CG1 VAL CB CG1 HG11 HG12 HG13
V_CG2 VAL CB CG2 HG21 HG22 HG23

#ACE/NME: standard N-/C-terminal capping groups (acetyl / N-methylamide),
#used instead of NTER/CTER on a capped peptide. Verified against real
#connectivity (mdtraj on a real ACE/NME-capped peptide): ACE has no CA, so
#the next residue's own _PHI rule silently drops its "-CA" atom (missing,
#skipped per convention) -- the real -C/-O peptide-bond pairs it still
#finds are enough; nothing extra is needed on the ACE side beyond the two
#groups below. Same idea for NME on the C-terminal side.
ACE_C ACE CH3 C O +N
ACE_CH3 ACE C CH3 H1 H2 H3
NME_N NME -C N H C
NME_C NME N C H1 H2 H3
